The asserts are checking the following conditions:

1. If the return value is non-negative (i.e., the item is found in the list), then the last index of the item in the old array is less than or equal to the new array (i.e., the item is not added at a new position if the item is already in the list).
    
2. If the item does not exist in the old array list, then it does not exist in the new array list.
    
3. If the item does not exist in the new array list, then the count of items in both the old and new array lists is the same (i.e., the item is added if it does not exist in the list).
