When the IndexOf method in ArrayList class returns a non negative number, it means that the element x is found in the ArrayList. Therefore, the last index of x in the old ArrayList should be smaller or equal to the last index of x in the new ArrayList. This assertion ensures that the last index of x in the new ArrayList reflects the changes from the old one. If the return value of IndexOf method is negative, it means that x is not in the ArrayList, so there's no need for an assertion as per this condition.
